abstract: >-
  A hand-checkable proof that R(B_66, B_67) = 267, the case n = 67 of Wesley's conjecture
  R(B_{n-1}, B_n) = 4n - 1, first shown by Chung, Du and Wesley in the Station data of 24 August 2026
  by a 266-vertex certificate. Their graph is, up to isomorphism, a two-block circulant graph over
  Z_133 whose connection sets are unions of orbits of the cube roots of unity modulo 133. The
  repository holds the paper, a Lean 4 kernel check of the graph (standard axioms only), independent
  checks in C and Python, the isomorphism with the Station certificate, the search, and a dated
  priority check.
